<p>This week's chapter: <a href="/how-to-build-an-ai/name-and-build-your-agent/">Name and build your agent</a>. A model answers questions; an agent has a job, a name, and rules about how it works with you. You write one short profile in plain English and the thing you built starts asking before it answers. <strong>The film is up.</strong> Watch it here, then the written chapter has every step in text if you'd rather read it, or want to come back to a bit of it later.</p>

<p>Hi, and welcome. If you're curious how an AI actually gets built, and whether <em>you</em> could build one, this is a good place to start. This guide grows a chapter at a time, and you can read it at your own pace. You don't need any coding experience, and you don't need to finish all of it. Think of it as a gentle on-ramp, not a test.</p>

